{"case_id":"C098","maintenance_needed":true,"confidence":96,"change_types":["API protocol change","new input dimensions","new configuration/state-dependent behavior","attack-surface expansion"],"affected_functions":["ares_getaddrinfo","lookup_service","fake_addrinfo","next_lookup","ares__parse_into_addrinfo"],"reason":"The commit substantially changes the public ares_getaddrinfo path, but neither existing fuzz target invokes that API. Its hints parameter changes from struct ares_addrinfo to struct ares_addrinfo_hints, service-name and numeric-service processing is added, and new flags such as ARES_AI_NOSORT and ARES_AI_ENVHOSTS affect behavior. Although the existing reply fuzzer continues to reach the refactored A/AAAA parsing through ares_parse_a_reply and ares_parse_aaaa_reply, it cannot exercise the changed getaddrinfo inputs, channel lookup state, service resolution, or hint combinations.","evidence":["ares_getaddrinfo now accepts const struct ares_addrinfo_hints* and ares_addrinfo_callback instead of the previous types.","The new ares_addrinfo_hints exposes ai_flags, ai_family, ai_socktype, and ai_protocol, while ARES_AI_NOSORT and ARES_AI_ENVHOSTS are newly defined.","ares_getaddrinfo now processes the service argument through ARES_AI_NUMERICSERV, strtoul, and lookup_service, with the new ARES_ESERVICE result.","The new host_query stores channel->lookups and invokes next_lookup, introducing lookup sequencing and channel-dependent state.","ares-test-fuzz.c only calls ares_parse_*_reply functions, and ares-test-fuzz-name.c only calls ares_create_query with fixed class and type; neither calls ares_getaddrinfo."],"recommended_action":"Keep the existing parser targets, and add a dedicated ares_getaddrinfo fuzz target that initializes and destroys an ares channel, derives bounded node and service strings plus family/flag/hint combinations from the input, drives the asynchronous lookup processing to callback completion, and frees callback results with ares_freeaddrinfo."}
